<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Auto Backup rules (API 30 and below; 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml).

     Backup is DISABLED outright by android:allowBackup="false" in the manifest,
     so these rules are not consulted today. They are kept, and inverted to
     INCLUDE-ONLY, as a second line of defence: if anyone ever flips allowBackup
     back on, an empty include set backs up nothing, instead of the old
     exclude-only list silently resuming a whole-data-directory backup.

     The exclude-only version listed sovereign_geofences.xml and
     sovereign_push.xml and reasoned that the WebView's localStorage "is not
     under any backed-up domain". That was wrong: app_webview sits in the app's
     data directory and Auto Backup takes it by default — and that is where the
     E2EE identity seed, the session JWT, the web device private key and
     remembered unattended-access seeds actually live.

     Nothing here needs to survive a reinstall via backup: a device re-derives
     its state by logging in, and the identity seed is recoverable from the
     server-held wrap with the password or the recovery phrase. So the correct
     include set is empty. If something ever genuinely needs backing up, add one
     explicit <include> for that path and nothing else. -->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- Intentionally empty: include-only with no includes backs up nothing. -->
    <include domain="root" path="backup-nothing-placeholder" />
</full-backup-content>
